From f372c1b2fa41b08ca1cf1d69efa9d158bbd92b5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerome Wuerf <oss@scharom.de>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:29:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(jira): support scoped Atlassian API tokens via the
 api.atlassian.com gateway

Scoped Atlassian API tokens are rejected on the site host, so a Cloud site
could only be connected with an unscoped classic token. Add a 'cloud-scoped'
auth type: connect resolves the site's cloudId from /_edge/tenant_info, stores
https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/<cloudId> as the site's apiBaseUrl, and routes
every REST call (including attachment downloads reported on the site host)
through it while siteUrl keeps serving browse links. The email is optional in
this mode: with it the token is sent as Basic, without it as Bearer.

The connect dialog gains an "API token / Scoped API token" toggle for Cloud and
names the scopes to grant; the mode state, copy and toggles move into
jira-connect-mode.ts and jira-connect-mode-toggles.tsx to keep the dialog
under the component line budget.

Bitbucket already accepts scoped API tokens on api.bitbucket.org in both auth
modes, but a token missing the pull request write scope reads fine and then
fails PR creation with a 403 that was reported as "not authenticated". Split
the 403 into a scope hint, name the required scopes in the connect dialog and
docs, and mention the read:user scope on a rejected verification.

Closes #16486

